statement.p:
Suppose that
\displaystyle{ f(x+h)-f(x) = -3 h x^2  +    6 h x  +    6 h^2 x  +    7 h^2  -    6 h^3.
}

webwork-reps.pg:
## DESCRIPTION ## Definition of the Derivative ## ENDDESCRIPTION
## Tagged by YL
## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable) ## DBchapter(Differentiation) ## DBsection(Definition of the derivative) ## Institution(ASU) ## MLT(defDerNumGiven) ## MLTleader(1) ## Level(3) ## TitleText1('Calculus: Early Transcendentals') ## AuthorText1('Stewart') ## EditionText1('5') ## Section1('2.8') ## Problem1('') ## TitleText2('Calculus: Early Transcendentals') ## AuthorText2('Stewart') ## EditionText2('6') ## Section2('2.7') ## Problem2('') ## KEYWORDS('derivative', 'definition')
DOCUMENT(); # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros( "PGstandard.pl", "PGchoicemacros.pl", "PGML.pl", "PGcourse.pl" );
TEXT(beginproblem()); $showPartialCorrectAnswers = 1;
$a = non_zero_random(-8,8,1); $b = non_zero_random(-8,8,1); $c = non_zero_random(-8,8,1); $d = non_zero_random(-8,8,1); $f = non_zero_random(-8,8,1);
BEGIN_PGML Suppose that [`` f(x+h)-f(x) = [$a] h x^2 ? {[$b]} h x ? {[$c]} h^2 x ? {[$d]} h^2 ? {[$f]} h^3. ``]
Find [`f'(x)`].
[`f'(x) = `] [________]
END_PGML
@answers = (fun_cmp("$a*x**2 + $b*x", vars=>"x"));
ANS(@answers );
ENDDOCUMENT(); # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
